# Agent and migration staging. `_workspace/README.md` declares this surface as
# ignored-by-default with two tracked contract documents; without these rules
# that contract was prose only, and scripts writing into repo-support/ (grype
# database seeds, supply-chain verdicts, rehearsal records) showed up as
# untracked files waiting to be committed.
/_workspace/*
!/_workspace/README.md
!/_workspace/repo-support/
/_workspace/repo-support/*
!/_workspace/repo-support/README.md

# Graphify is optional generated intelligence for local exploration, and this
# rule now governs the whole directory. Forty-seven files under it were tracked
# while this line already ignored them, so a rebuild replaced a 148 MiB blob on
# every graph-touching commit and each new dated backup was ignored while the
# older ones were not. Rebuild locally with `graphify update .`, which costs no
# API tokens; Git history holds the snapshots that were removed. Patterns under
# an ignored directory are dead, so `cache/`, `manifest.json`, and `cost.json`
# no longer need their own lines. Re-tracking anything here needs `git add -f`
# and a stated reason.
graphify-out/
